#: src/semantic-tokens.md:1
msgid "Semantic Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:3
msgid ""
"Semantic tokens provide richer syntax highlighting by using information from "
"language servers. Unlike tree-sitter highlighting, which is based purely on "
"syntax, semantic tokens understand the meaning of your code—distinguishing "
"between local variables and parameters, or between a class definition and a "
"class reference."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:5
msgid "Enabling Semantic Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:7
msgid ""
"Semantic tokens are controlled by the `semantic_tokens` setting. By default, "
"semantic tokens are disabled."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:11 src/semantic-tokens.md:27
#: src/semantic-tokens.md:30 src/semantic-tokens.md:33
msgid "\"semantic_tokens\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:11 src/semantic-tokens.md:30
msgid "\"combined\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:15
msgid "This setting accepts three values:"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:17
msgid "Value"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:17 src/semantic-tokens.md:52
#: src/semantic-tokens.md:154
msgid "Description"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:19
msgid "`\"off\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:19
msgid ""
"Do not request semantic tokens from language servers. Uses tree-sitter "
"highlighting only. (Default)"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:20
msgid "`\"combined\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:20
msgid ""
"Use LSP semantic tokens together with tree-sitter highlighting. Tree-sitter "
"provides base highlighting, and semantic tokens overlay additional "
"information."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:21
msgid "`\"full\"`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:21
msgid ""
"Use LSP semantic tokens exclusively. Tree-sitter highlighting is disabled "
"entirely for buffers with semantic token support."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:23
msgid "You can configure this globally or per-language:"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:27
msgid "\"off\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:28
msgid "\"languages\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:29
msgid "\"Rust\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:32
msgid "\"TypeScript\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:33
msgid "\"full\""
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:39
msgid ""
"**Note:** Changing the `semantic_tokens` mode may require a language server "
"restart to take effect. Use the `lsp: restart language servers` command from "
"the command palette if highlighting doesn't update immediately."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:41
msgid "Customizing Token Colors"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:43
msgid ""
"Semantic tokens are styled using rules that map LSP token types and "
"modifiers to theme styles or custom colors. Zed provides sensible defaults, "
"but you can customize these in your settings.json: add rules under "
"`global_lsp_settings.semantic_token_rules` key."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:45
msgid ""
"Rules are matched in order, and the first matching rule wins. User-defined "
"rules take precedence over defaults."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:48
msgid "Rule Structure"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:50
msgid "Each rule can specify:"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:52
msgid "Property"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:54
msgid "`token_type`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:54
msgid ""
"The LSP semantic token type to match (e.g., `\"variable\"`, `\"function\"`, "
"`\"class\"`). If omitted, matches all types."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:55
msgid "`token_modifiers`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:55
msgid ""
"A list of modifiers that must all be present (e.g., `[\"declaration\"]`, "
"`[\"readonly\", \"static\"]`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:56
msgid "`style`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:56
msgid ""
"A list of theme style names to try. The first one found in the current theme "
"is used."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:57
msgid "`foreground_color`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:57
msgid "Override foreground color in hex format (e.g., `\"#ff0000\"`)."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:58
msgid "`background_color`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:58
msgid "Override background color in hex format."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:59
msgid "`underline`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:59
msgid "Boolean or hex color. If `true`, underlines with the text color."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:60
msgid "`strikethrough`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:60
msgid "Boolean or hex color. If `true`, strikes through with the text color."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:61
msgid "`font_weight`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:61
msgid "`\"normal\"` or `\"bold\"`."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:62
msgid "`font_style`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:62
msgid "`\"normal\"` or `\"italic\"`."
msgstr ""

