msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:180
msgid "Inspecting Semantic Tokens"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:182
msgid ""
"To see semantic tokens applied to your code in real-time, use the `dev: open "
"highlights tree view` command from the command palette. This opens a panel "
"showing all highlights (including semantic tokens) for the current buffer, "
"making it easier to understand which tokens are being applied and debug your "
"custom rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:184
msgid "Troubleshooting"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:186
msgid "Semantic highlighting not appearing"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:188
msgid ""
"Ensure `semantic_tokens` is set to `\"combined\"` or `\"full\"` for the "
"language"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:189
msgid "Verify the language server supports semantic tokens (not all do)"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:190
msgid "Try restarting the language server with `lsp: restart language servers`"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:191
msgid "Check the LSP logs (`workspace: open lsp log`) for errors"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:193
msgid "Colors not updating after changing settings"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:195
msgid ""
"Changes to `semantic_tokens` mode may require a language server restart. Use "
"`lsp: restart language servers` from the command palette."
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:197
msgid "Theme styles not being applied"
msgstr ""

#: src/semantic-tokens.md:199
msgid ""
"Ensure the style names in your rules match styles defined in your theme. The "
"`style` array provides fallback options—if the first style isn't found, Zed "
"tries the next one."
msgstr ""
